{
 "id": "8nHBGFKLHZQ",
 "path": "invidious-mirror",
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 3.19,
   "text": "What would happen to you if"
  },
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 3.19,
   "text": "a black hole the size of a coin"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.201,
   "duration": 1.63,
   "text": "suddenly appeared near you?"
  },
  {
   "start": 4.836,
   "duration": 1.51,
   "text": "Short answer: you\u2019d die."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.351,
   "duration": 1.73,
   "text": "Long answer: it depends."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.081,
   "duration": 1.88,
   "text": "Is it a black hole with"
  },
  {
   "start": 8.081,
   "duration": 1.88,
   "text": "the mass of a coin,"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.963,
   "duration": 1.54,
   "text": "or is it as wide as a coin?"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.503,
   "duration": 3.46,
   "text": "Suppose a US nickel with"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.503,
   "duration": 3.46,
   "text": "the mass of about 5 grams"
  },
  {
   "start": 14.963,
   "duration": 2.12,
   "text": "magically collapsed into a black hole."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.083,
   "duration": 3.56,
   "text": "This black hole would have a radius"
  },
  {
   "start": 17.083,
   "duration": 3.56,
   "text": "of about 10 to the power of \u221230 meters."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.645,
   "duration": 4.82,
   "text": "By comparison, a hydrogen atom is about"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.645,
   "duration": 4.82,
   "text": "10 to the power of \u221211 meters."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.465,
   "duration": 2.99,
   "text": "So the black hole compared"
  },
  {
   "start": 25.465,
   "duration": 2.99,
   "text": "to an atom is as small as"
  },
  {
   "start": 28.455,
   "duration": 1.76,
   "text": "an atom compared to the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.215,
   "duration": 1.67,
   "text": "Unimaginably small!"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.885,
   "duration": 3.79,
   "text": "And a small black hole would also have"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.885,
   "duration": 3.79,
   "text": "an unimaginably short lifetime"
  },
  {
   "start": 35.675,
   "duration": 1.61,
   "text": "to decay by Hawking radiation."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.285,
   "duration": 5.17,
   "text": "It would radiate away what little mass it"
  },
  {
   "start": 37.285,
   "duration": 5.17,
   "text": "has in 10 to the power of \u221223 seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.455,
   "duration": 4.77,
   "text": "Its 5 grams of mass will be converted"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.455,
   "duration": 4.77,
   "text": "to 450 terajoules of energy,"
  },
  {
   "start": 47.225,
   "duration": 3.021,
   "text": "which will lead to an explosion"
  },
  {
   "start": 47.225,
   "duration": 3.021,
   "text": "roughly 3 times bigger than"
  },
  {
   "start": 50.246,
   "duration": 3.37,
   "text": "the atomic bombs dropped on"
  },
  {
   "start": 50.246,
   "duration": 3.37,
   "text": "Hiroshima and Nagasaki combined."
  },
  {
   "start": 53.627,
   "duration": 1.47,
   "text": "In this case, you die."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.097,
   "duration": 1.98,
   "text": "You also lose the coin."
  },
  {
   "start": 57.092,
   "duration": 2.78,
   "text": "If the black hole had the"
  },
  {
   "start": 57.092,
   "duration": 2.78,
   "text": "diameter of a common coin,"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.88,
   "duration": 2.253,
   "text": "then it would be considerably"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.88,
   "duration": 2.253,
   "text": "more massive."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.133,
   "duration": 3.132,
   "text": "In fact, a black hole with"
  },
  {
   "start": 62.133,
   "duration": 3.132,
   "text": "the diameter of a nickel"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.265,
   "duration": 2.21,
   "text": "would be slightly more"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.265,
   "duration": 2.21,
   "text": "massive than the Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.475,
   "duration": 3.72,
   "text": "It would have a surface gravity"
  },
  {
   "start": 67.475,
   "duration": 3.72,
   "text": "a billion billion times greater"
  },
  {
   "start": 71.195,
   "duration": 1.7,
   "text": "than our planet currently does."
  },
  {
   "start": 72.895,
   "duration": 2.58,
   "text": "Its tidal forces on you would be so strong"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.483,
   "duration": 2.84,
   "text": "that they\u2019d rip your"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.483,
   "duration": 2.84,
   "text": "individual cells apart."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.323,
   "duration": 4.07,
   "text": "The black hole would consume you before"
  },
  {
   "start": 78.323,
   "duration": 4.07,
   "text": "you even realized what\u2019s happening."
  },
  {
   "start": 82.393,
   "duration": 2.26,
   "text": "Although the laws of gravity"
  },
  {
   "start": 82.393,
   "duration": 2.26,
   "text": "are still the same,"
  },
  {
   "start": 84.657,
   "duration": 3.35,
   "text": "the phenomenon of gravity that you\u2019d"
  },
  {
   "start": 84.657,
   "duration": 3.35,
   "text": "experience would be very different"
  },
  {
   "start": 88.007,
   "duration": 1.84,
   "text": "around such dense objects."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.87,
   "duration": 1.82,
   "text": "The range of the gravitational attraction"
  },
  {
   "start": 91.702,
   "duration": 2.27,
   "text": "extends over the entire"
  },
  {
   "start": 91.702,
   "duration": 2.27,
   "text": "observable universe,"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.972,
   "duration": 3.2,
   "text": "with gravity getting weaker the farther"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.972,
   "duration": 3.2,
   "text": "away you are from something."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.172,
   "duration": 4.49,
   "text": "On Earth right now, your head and your"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.172,
   "duration": 4.49,
   "text": "toes are approximately the same distance"
  },
  {
   "start": 101.662,
   "duration": 1.46,
   "text": "from the center of our planet."
  },
  {
   "start": 103.122,
   "duration": 2.57,
   "text": "But if you stood on"
  },
  {
   "start": 103.122,
   "duration": 2.57,
   "text": "a nickel-sized black hole,"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.692,
   "duration": 2.79,
   "text": "your feet would be hundreds"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.692,
   "duration": 2.79,
   "text": "of times closer to the center,"
  },
  {
   "start": 108.482,
   "duration": 3.74,
   "text": "and the gravitational force would be"
  },
  {
   "start": 108.482,
   "duration": 3.74,
   "text": "tens of thousands of times as large"
  },
  {
   "start": 112.231,
   "duration": 3.45,
   "text": "as the force on your head and"
  },
  {
   "start": 112.231,
   "duration": 3.45,
   "text": "rip you into a billion pieces."
  },
  {
   "start": 115.681,
   "duration": 2.49,
   "text": "But the black hole wouldn\u2019t"
  },
  {
   "start": 115.681,
   "duration": 2.49,
   "text": "stop with just you."
  },
  {
   "start": 118.171,
   "duration": 3.29,
   "text": "The black hole is now a"
  },
  {
   "start": 118.171,
   "duration": 3.29,
   "text": "dominant gravitational piece"
  },
  {
   "start": 121.461,
   "duration": 2.59,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "start": 121.461,
   "duration": 2.59,
   "text": "Earth\u2013Moon\u2013Black-Hole-of-Death system."
  },
  {
   "start": 124.051,
   "duration": 3.71,
   "text": "You might think that the black hole would"
  },
  {
   "start": 124.051,
   "duration": 3.71,
   "text": "sink towards the center of the planet"
  },
  {
   "start": 127.761,
   "duration": 2.34,
   "text": "and consume it from the inside out."
  },
  {
   "start": 130.101,
   "duration": 4.53,
   "text": "In fact, the Earth also moves up onto"
  },
  {
   "start": 130.101,
   "duration": 4.53,
   "text": "the black hole and begins to bob around,"
  },
  {
   "start": 134.631,
   "duration": 1.7,
   "text": "as if it were orbiting the black hole,"
  },
  {
   "start": 136.331,
   "duration": 2.74,
   "text": "all while having swathes of"
  },
  {
   "start": 136.331,
   "duration": 2.74,
   "text": "mass eaten with each pass,"
  },
  {
   "start": 139.071,
   "duration": 1.62,
   "text": "which is much more creepy."
  },
  {
   "start": 141.049,
   "duration": 2.51,
   "text": "As the Earth is eaten up from the inside,"
  },
  {
   "start": 143.559,
   "duration": 2.54,
   "text": "it collapses into a"
  },
  {
   "start": 143.559,
   "duration": 2.54,
   "text": "scattered disk of hot rock,"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.099,
   "duration": 2.26,
   "text": "surrounding the black hole"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.099,
   "duration": 2.26,
   "text": "in a tight orbit."
  },
  {
   "start": 148.359,
   "duration": 3.5,
   "text": "The black hole slowly doubles its mass"
  },
  {
   "start": 148.359,
   "duration": 3.5,
   "text": "by the time it\u2019s done feeding."
  },
  {
   "start": 151.859,
   "duration": 2.95,
   "text": "The Moon\u2019s orbit is now highly elliptical."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.809,
   "duration": 2.48,
   "text": "The effects on the Solar system"
  },
  {
   "start": 154.809,
   "duration": 2.48,
   "text": "are awesome\u2014"
  },
  {
   "start": 157.289,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "in the Biblical sense of awesome,"
  },
  {
   "start": 157.289,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "which means terrifying."
  },
  {
   "start": 161.298,
   "duration": 3.76,
   "text": "Tidal forces from the black hole would"
  },
  {
   "start": 161.298,
   "duration": 3.76,
   "text": "probably disrupt the near-Earth asteroids,"
  },
  {
   "start": 165.058,
   "duration": 2.34,
   "text": "maybe even parts of the asteroid belt,"
  },
  {
   "start": 167.42,
   "duration": 2.42,
   "text": "sending rocks careening"
  },
  {
   "start": 167.42,
   "duration": 2.42,
   "text": "through the Solar system."
  },
  {
   "start": 169.847,
   "duration": 2.83,
   "text": "Bombardment and impacts"
  },
  {
   "start": 169.847,
   "duration": 2.83,
   "text": "may become commonplace"
  },
  {
   "start": 172.677,
   "duration": 1.48,
   "text": "for the next few million years."
  },
  {
   "start": 174.157,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "The planets are slightly perturbed, but"
  },
  {
   "start": 174.157,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "stay approximately in the same orbit."
  },
  {
   "start": 178.157,
   "duration": 2.7,
   "text": "The black hole we used"
  },
  {
   "start": 178.157,
   "duration": 2.7,
   "text": "to call Earth will now"
  },
  {
   "start": 180.857,
   "duration": 2.5,
   "text": "continue on orbiting"
  },
  {
   "start": 180.857,
   "duration": 2.5,
   "text": "the Sun in the Earth\u2019s place."
  },
  {
   "start": 183.363,
   "duration": 2.66,
   "text": "In this case, you also die."
  },
  {
   "start": 187.934,
   "duration": 3.19,
   "text": "This bonus video was made possible"
  },
  {
   "start": 187.934,
   "duration": 3.19,
   "text": "by your contributions on Patreon."
  },
  {
   "start": 191.536,
   "duration": 2.05,
   "text": "Thank you so much for your support!"
  },
  {
   "start": 194.098,
   "duration": 3.18,
   "text": "The topic is based on a question on"
  },
  {
   "start": 194.098,
   "duration": 3.18,
   "text": "the AskScience subreddit"
  },
  {
   "start": 197.278,
   "duration": 4.29,
   "text": "and the glorious answer by Matt [Caplin?],"
  },
  {
   "start": 197.278,
   "duration": 4.29,
   "text": "who also worked with us on this video."
  },
  {
   "start": 202.023,
   "duration": 3.58,
   "text": "Check out his blog, Quarks and Coffee,"
  },
  {
   "start": 202.023,
   "duration": 3.58,
   "text": "for more awesome stuff like this!"
  },
  {
   "start": 205.757,
   "duration": 3.32,
   "text": "If you want to discuss the video,"
  },
  {
   "start": 205.757,
   "duration": 3.32,
   "text": "we have our own subreddit now."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.643,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "To learn more about black holes or equally"
  },
  {
   "start": 209.643,
   "duration": 4.0,
   "text": "interesting neutron stars, click here."
  },
  {
   "start": 215.0,
   "duration": 3.0,
   "text": "Subtitles by the Amara.org community"
  }
 ]
}